## Quick Start

```bash
# Start the development server
docker compose up --build

# The API is available at http://localhost:8001/api/v1
# Admin panel at http://localhost:8001/admin/
```

## Commands

All commands run inside the Docker container:

```bash
docker compose exec app python manage.py startapp <name>       # Scaffold a new app
docker compose exec app python manage.py makemigrations [msg]  # Generate a migration
docker compose exec app python manage.py migrate               # Apply migrations
docker compose exec app python manage.py shell                 # IPython shell
docker compose exec app python manage.py createsuperuser       # Create an admin user
docker compose exec app python -m pytest                       # Run tests
```

### Running the tests

`AUTH_USER_MODEL_TYPE` fixes the shape of the `User` model when it is imported,
so a pytest process runs under one auth mode. Run the suite once per mode:

```bash
docker compose exec app python -m pytest
docker compose exec -e AUTH_USER_MODEL_TYPE=email app python -m pytest
```

The default test database is in-memory SQLite. Before calling a database change
done, run against PostgreSQL — teardown deadlocks, stale table shapes and
foreign-key ordering bugs are invisible on SQLite:

```bash
docker compose exec db psql -U "$DB_USER" -d "$DB_NAME" \
    -c "CREATE DATABASE test_db OWNER $DB_USER;"
docker compose exec \
    -e TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql+asyncpg://$DB_USER:$DB_PASSWORD@db:5432/test_db" \
    app python -m pytest
```

