## Configuration

All settings are in `app/djast/settings.py` and can be overridden via environment variables in `dev.env` (development) or `prod.env` (production).

See `prod.env.example` for production configuration reference.

`copier copy` generated a unique `SECRET_KEY` and `DB_PASSWORD` into `dev.env`.
**`prod.env` is yours to fill in** — nothing generates its secrets. The app
refuses to start while `SECRET_KEY` or `DB_PASSWORD` still holds a value that
ships with the template.

## Migrations

`migrations/` and `alembic.ini` are tracked by this repository on purpose: a
production deploy runs `manage.py migrate` and never `makemigrations`, so the
migration history has to travel with the code. Do not add them to `.gitignore`
or `.dockerignore`.

## Background tasks

Define tasks in `<app>/tasks.py`. The worker discovers every one of them
(`--fs-discover --tasks-pattern "*/tasks.py"` in the compose files) — a task
defined anywhere else is never registered, and enqueuing it succeeds silently.
After adding an app with tasks, confirm once:

```bash
docker compose logs taskiq-worker | grep Importing
```

